# No Cursor co-author on commits

When creating a git commit, do not add Cursor (or any Cursor agent identity) as a co-author.

- Do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- Do not add any other `Co-authored-by` line for Cursor, Cursor Agent, or similar
- Commit message body is the change description only

```text
# BAD
Fix the mapping review crash.

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# GOOD
Fix the mapping review crash.
```
